# LF everywhere, in the repository and in every working copy.
#
# Two things depend on it. The Makefile's recipes break under CRLF, and a
# Windows checkout converts them by default. And degenerator writes generated
# files as bytes with explicit \n, so a source tree that drifted to CRLF would
# make the tool's own line endings inconsistent with what it emits.
* text=auto eol=lf
